## 4. Mandatory Syntax Verification & Dynamic JS Generation Pitfalls (Lessons Learned)

To prevent low-level errors (e.g., syntax errors, broken regexes, or a blank white screen on app launch), every AI Agent **MUST** strictly adhere to the following rules:

### Rule D: Mandatory Static Syntax Check (`node -c`)
Whenever you modify `localization_engine.js` or any `scripts/*.js` file:
```powershell
node -c localization_engine.js
node -c scripts/dev_tool.js
node -c scripts/compare_dicts.js
```

### Rule E: Dynamic JS Injection Safety (`generateJs()` Pitfalls & White Screen Prevention)
`localization_engine.js` uses `generateJs()` to dynamically construct the JavaScript code (`preload.js`) injected into `app.asar`.
1. **DOUBLE-ESCAPE Regex Backslashes inside `jsSource` (CRITICAL!):**
   Inside `generateJs()`, `const jsSource = \`...\`` is a template literal evaluated by Node.js!
   - If you write single backslashes like `/\s+\./` inside `jsSource`, Node.js swallows the single backslash and emits `/s+./` (matching the letter `s` and any char!) into `preload.js`.
   - You **MUST ALWAYS double-escape backslashes** in regexes and strings inside `jsSource`: write `\\s`, `\\.`, `\\d`, `\\b`, `\\(`, `\\)`.
2. **NO Raw Template Interpolation or Hardcoded Local Paths inside `jsSource`:**
   - **DO NOT** write `${name}` inside `jsSource`; always use string concatenation `+ name +`.
   - **NEVER** hardcode personal local workspace paths (e.g., `e:/OneDrive/...`) inside `generateJs()`.
   - Always use functional replacement `jsSource.replace("DICT_PLACEHOLDER", () => dictJson)` so `$` characters in dictionaries are never interpreted as regex replacement patterns.
3. **Mandatory Generated Code Verification in Project Root (Both SC and TC):**
   - **WARNING:** Never write the temporary test script inside `scratch/` when testing `generateJs()`, because `loadDictionary()` resolves `path.join(__dirname, DICTS_FOLDER)`. Writing it in the project root (`./_temp_root_test.js`) ensures the real 3,900+ dictionary entries are loaded and tested!
   ```powershell
   node -e 'const fs=require("fs"); const code=fs.readFileSync("localization_engine.js","utf8").replace(/main\(\);/,"module.exports={generateJs};"); fs.writeFileSync("_temp_root_test.js",code); const {generateJs}=require("./_temp_root_test.js"); fs.unlinkSync("_temp_root_test.js"); const out=generateJs(); new Function(out); console.log("Generated JS syntax check OK! Size:", (out.length/1024).toFixed(1)+"KB");'
   node -e 'process.argv.push("--tw"); const fs=require("fs"); const code=fs.readFileSync("localization_engine.js","utf8").replace(/main\(\);/,"module.exports={generateJs};"); fs.writeFileSync("_temp_root_test_tw.js",code); const {generateJs}=require("./_temp_root_test_tw.js"); fs.unlinkSync("_temp_root_test_tw.js"); const out=generateJs(); new Function(out); console.log("Generated TW JS syntax check OK! Size:", (out.length/1024).toFixed(1)+"KB");'
   ```
   Verify that `Size` is **~290KB+** (confirming dictionaries loaded properly) and `new Function(out)` throws zero errors.

### Rule G: DOM Fragmentation, Short Words & Community PR Audit (Anti-Pollution Rule)
1. **DO NOT add generic single words or broken fragments into global dictionaries:**
   - Never add generic single words (`<= 15` chars without spaces, e.g. `"Type"`, `"Use"`, `"Variables"`, `"Selection"`) or broken sentence fragments starting/ending with punctuation/prepositions (e.g. `", then reopen this dialog."`, `"to upload"`, `"tokens ("`) into `dicts/` or `dicts_tw/`.
   - Handle fragmented DOM sentences inside `generateJs()` by inspecting `node.parentElement` context first.
2. **Strict Audit SOP for External / Community PRs:**
   Never blindly merge external dictionary PRs. Before merging any PR, you **MUST**:
   - Deduplicate against all existing `dicts/*.json` keys so existing standardized translations are never overwritten.
   - Verify candidate keys against the live client bundle (`main.js`) and strip out VS Code 1.0 dead strings or Monaco internal schema descriptions (e.g. `background color`, `foreground color`, `activity bar`, `minimap`, `overview ruler`).
   - Sanitize all `dicts_tw/` values against the Forbidden Mainland Terms table in Section 3 and run `node scripts/compare_dicts.js`.

---

## 5. Client Architecture & Zero-Screenshot Version Upgrade SOP (v2.27.0+)
Antigravity 2.x utilizes a two-tier architecture:
- **Main Process:** Electron process loaded from `resources/app.asar` (`dist/main.js`, `dist/preload.js`, `dist/menu.js`, `dist/tray.js`).
- **Frontend SPA:** Managed by `resources/bin/language_server.exe` which serves the live SPA on `https://127.0.0.1:<PORT>/main.js`.

### Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) When User Reports an Antigravity Upgrade:
The user does **NOT** need to take screenshots when Antigravity upgrades. Follow these exact steps:
1. **Step 1 — Scan UI & Hover Tooltips Diff:**
   ```powershell
   node scripts/dev_tool.js scan-ui
   ```
   This automatically connects to the running `language_server`, extracts all UI strings & mouse hover tooltips (`title`, `aria-label`, `placeholder`, `tooltip`, `<Rz>`, JSX children), diffs them against `scripts/ui_strings_baseline.json`, checks coverage against `dicts/*.json`, and outputs untranslated strings to `scratch/untranslated_ui_diff.json`.
2. **Step 2 — Scan Official MCP Catalog Diff:**
   ```powershell
   node scripts/dev_tool.js dump-mcp
   ```
   Checks live RPC `GetAvailableCascadePlugins` against `scripts/mcp_catalog_baseline.json` and outputs any new/changed MCP servers to `scratch/mcp_catalog_diff.json`.
3. **Step 3 — Translate & Update Baselines:**
   - Read `scratch/untranslated_ui_diff.json` and `scratch/mcp_catalog_diff.json`.
   - Filter out code tokens/single generic words (Rule G), and add genuine new UI/tooltip/MCP entries to both `dicts/` and `dicts_tw/`.
   - Update baselines and clean up `scratch/`:
     ```powershell
     node scripts/dev_tool.js scan-ui --update-baseline
     node scripts/dev_tool.js dump-mcp --update-baseline
     Remove-Item -Path scratch\* -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
     ```
4. **Other `dev_tool.js` Diagnostic Commands:**
   - `node scripts/dev_tool.js port` (detects running `language_server` PID, ports, and CSRF token on Windows & macOS)
   - `node scripts/dev_tool.js search <keyword>` (searches live `main.js` context)
   - `node scripts/dev_tool.js slice <pos> [len]` (inspects exact bundle slices)

---

## 6. Pre-Delivery Checklist
Before reporting task completion to the user, you **MUST** verify all five items:
- [x] `node -c localization_engine.js` and `node -c scripts/dev_tool.js` pass with 0 errors.
- [x] Root `new Function(generateJs())` syntax check passes on both SC and TC output (Size ~290KB+).
- [x] `node scripts/compare_dicts.js` prints `All dictionaries are perfectly aligned!` (0 missing keys, 0 SC leaks in TC).
- [x] `scratch/` directory is clean of temporary scripts/dumps.
- [x] Windows `.bat` files preserve CRLF + GBK/Big5; macOS `.command` files preserve LF + UTF-8 (no BOM) + `100755`.
